paragraph('Legal FPGA routes trade timing, wire and vertical resources.',r'''Legal routing trades timing, wire and vertical resources. Current-STA transactional repair selects groups, applies retained-crossing domains with per-net failed-search release, and coordinates blocking owners before whole-candidate checks. Matched complete BNN flows reach 13.228146 ns in 7933.25/9754.31 s: domain-first spends 1786 wire for 39 fewer SB/two fewer CB. Three timing repairs improve strong native CPD by 2.787376\%. Local owner controls establish coordination effects; a fixed-scope robot union separates domain-induced tradeoffs from release-enabled feasibility. Transfer includes no-gain, routing-failure and execution-timeout inputs. A prospective frozen conv-hls pair confirms a no-op, not positive controller benefit. Symmetric engineering and complete costs remain essential to assessing these tradeoffs.''')
