paragraph('Combining lazy scheduling with in-call source snapshots preserves', '')
paragraph('The new robot input changes actual placement',r'''A distinct robot placement with explicit 20-ns clock and 1/0-ns maximum/minimum I/O constraints has identical initial/final vectors in both arms: 12.727250365 ns, 250411/2/526. All 10972 setup/hold components are finite/nonnegative. No sharing/owner cut qualifies; all three timing proposals fail acceptance. The fastest legal proposal, 12.671110383 ns, exceeds wire/SB/CB limits by 8/1/1. Both retain the root at 498.00/504.09 s. This benchmark SDC is not an external application requirement. Attention fails initial routing after 200 iterations with 231 overused nodes in both arms (794.67/792.69 s). Four roles yield one legal physical pair, not independent arm samples.''')
paragraph('Robot native/domain reach 251116/251136 wire',r'''Robot native/domain reach 251116/251136 wire, 9/9 SB, 653/652 CB at 13.354624073 ns in 377.71/424.45 s: domain spends 20 wire and 46.74 s for one CB. Both conv-layer roles fail initial routing within 200 iterations (260.10/254.57 s). The cohort has two legal outputs among four roles; historical ``heldout'' directory names do not establish unseen testing.''')
paragraph('Single-pass indexing preserves BNN graph payloads',r'''Single-pass indexing preserves BNN graph payloads, states, requests and native work at 7463.17 versus 7933.25 s. Metadata reuse/streaming preserves native execution at 7247 s (qualified GNU-time; observer/PSS lost, brief overlap). The same changes preserve domain states, requests, work and full vectors at 9116.40 versus 9754.31 s, a descriptive 637.92-s/6.54\% reduction; sampled PSS is 11.067 GiB with 28 missing observations. This establishes behavior preservation, not statistical acceleration or an optimized N/D ratio. Original matched overhead remains 22.95\%; symmetric interleaving is running.''')
